  "published": "2026-10-25T20:52:13.23Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.2.0: Multi-targeting release. The package now ships net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 assets instead of net8.0 only. Cross-repo dependencies are refreshed to CoreSystem.Http 1.2.0, CoreSystem.Memory 1.1.0, CoreSystem.Resilience 2.1.0 and CoreSystem.Serialization 1.3.0, which is what removes the NU1605 restore failure on net10.0 described in 2.1.3: earlier Resilience versions constrained Microsoft.Extensions.* to 8.0.x while OpenTelemetry asks for 10.0.0. Verified with real net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 consumer projects: all three restore and resolve with no workaround. This build still declares CoreSystem.Cache 3.0.2 because that is the version on the feed while it is prepared; the pin moves to 3.1.0 once that version is published. No public API changed, nothing is renamed and no code changed. The AddHealthChecks() prerequisite still applies: RehydrationService takes a HealthCheckService, so without it the host fails to start, and without a primary-tagged check rehydration silently never runs.",
